  "notes": "### Fixed\n- **Round-table agents no longer time out before they speak** — a round table starts every seat at once, and each mirror had only 30 seconds to come up and accept its turn (Codex: 20 seconds to start, then 30 for its thread). With several CLIs launching side by side, and Windows scanning each one as it starts, seats failed with \"timed out waiting for initialize\" or \"thread/start\" without saying a word. They now get two minutes to start, the same patience the main Codex lane has, and if one still does not come up the message says it never started.",
